<title>GERMANY: Pan-German Nov industry orders rise 0.5 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>Pan-German Nov industry orders rise 0.5 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The economics ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> PAN-GERMAN INDUSTRY ORDERS  Nov 96     Oct 96	Nov 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change	  +0.5	 +2.7(+2.9)  +3.1</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +3.6	 +6.3(+6.4)   n/a</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		99.1	 98.6(98.7)  95.7</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted and provisional and expressed in volume terms. Year-on-year changes are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank data.  </p>
<p>The ministry gave the following month-on-month details:</p>
<p>				     Nov 96     Oct 96    Nov 96 index</p>
<p> Total domestic orders	  +1.1	 +2.1	  91.5</p>
<p> Total foreign orders	   -0.4	 +3.7	 114.4</p>
<p> Intermediate goods	     -0.6	 +2.1	 101.8</p>
<p> Of which: domestic	     -0.4	 +1.5	  94.8</p>
<p>	     foreign		-0.8	 +2.7	 117.9</p>
<p> Capital goods		    +2.4	 +4.0	 100.9</p>
<p> Of which: domestic	     +4.1	 +4.8	  92.4</p>
<p>	     foreign		+0.3	 +3.0	 114.8</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables     unch	 +2.2	  89.4</p>
<p> Of which: domestic	     +0.6	 -1.0	  81.8</p>
<p>	     foreign		-1.2	 +7.9	 105.3</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Oct/Nov 96 with Aug/Sept 96:</p>
<p> Industrial orders		     +1.0</p>
<p> Domestic orders			 +1.5</p>
<p> Foreign orders			  +1.0</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		    +1.0</p>
<p> Capital goods			   +2.5</p>
<p>    Of which, domestic		 +4.5</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables	    -1.0</p>
<p>Two month comparison Oct/Nov 96 with Oct/Nov 95:</p>
<p> Industrial orders		     +5.0</p>
<p> Domestic orders			 +0.8</p>
<p> Foreign orders			 +12.7</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		    +7.8</p>
<p> Capital goods			   +2.7</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables	    +2.0</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097-150</p>
</text>
